      "id": 1,
      "text": "Macomb Township was named for General Alexander Macomb, a War of 1812 hero whose mercantile family once owned most of the county.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Macomb_Township%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "German farmers were drawn to Macomb’s flat, fertile land by the Clinton River, and their cultural imprint still echoes today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Macomb_Township%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Romeo Plank Road, a historic route, traces the western side of the Clinton River through Macomb.",
