        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Macomb_Township%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Legislative Council approved Macomb Township on March 7, 1834, officially establishing the community that day.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Macomb_Township%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In the late 1800s, logs were floated south from Wolcott Mill down the Middle Branch of the Clinton River to sawmills in Macomb.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Macomb_Township%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Macomb sits at the geographic center of Macomb County, just 7 mi north of Mount Clemens and 26 mi north of Detroit.",
